  "caption": "Quinn's first steps out of bed were pure robot mode. So Quinn rested the Achilles for three weeks on the couch, and the first run back still hurt.\n\nRest can calm an irritated tendon, but it does little to build the capacity running needs. Tendons often respond to gradual loading, and change usually takes months.\n\nWhat often helps: slow calf raises that progress to heavier work and hops, using next-day symptoms as a guide, trimming hills and speed before stopping runs, and going easy on forceful stretching.\n\nA snap or pop, a gap in the tendon, major swelling or suddenly not being able to push off need prompt medical assessment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
